{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794861188683,"sessionID":"ses_e19f1290fffeOm13DSw4yBRd3L","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_518de2f2e6ab4d96826374a1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py","oldString":"        if self._dom_restricted and self._dow_restricted:\n            # Both restricted: either one may select the day.\n            return day_of_month_ok or day_of_week_ok\n        if self._dom_restricted:\n            return day_of_week_ok\n        if self._dow_restricted:\n            return day_of_month_ok\n        return True","newString":"        if self._dom_restricted and self._dow_restricted:\n            # Both restricted: either one may select the day.\n            return day_of_month_ok or day_of_week_ok\n        if self._dom_restricted:\n            # The day of week field is \"*\", so only the day of month counts.\n            return day_of_month_ok\n        if self._dow_restricted:\n            # The day of month field is \"*\", so only the day of week counts.\n            return day_of_week_ok\n        return True"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py\n@@ -56,11 +56,13 @@\n     if self._dom_restricted and self._dow_restricted:\n         # Both restricted: either one may select the day.\n         return day_of_month_ok or day_of_week_ok\n     if self._dom_restricted:\n-        return day_of_week_ok\n-    if self._dow_restricted:\n+        # The day of week field is \"*\", so only the day of month counts.\n         return day_of_month_ok\n+    if self._dow_restricted:\n+        # The day of month field is \"*\", so only the day of week counts.\n+        return day_of_week_ok\n     return True\n \n def _next_month_start(self, moment: datetime) -> datetime:\n     \"\"\"Return midnight of the first day of the next matching month.\"\"\"\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py","patch":"Index: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py\n@@ -56,11 +56,13 @@\n     if self._dom_restricted and self._dow_restricted:\n         # Both restricted: either one may select the day.\n         return day_of_month_ok or day_of_week_ok\n     if self._dom_restricted:\n-        return day_of_week_ok\n-    if self._dow_restricted:\n+        # The day of week field is \"*\", so only the day of month counts.\n         return day_of_month_ok\n+    if self._dow_restricted:\n+        # The day of month field is \"*\", so only the day of week counts.\n+        return day_of_week_ok\n     return True\n \n def _next_month_start(self, moment: datetime) -> datetime:\n     \"\"\"Return midnight of the first day of the next matching month.\"\"\"\n","additions":4,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/cron-scheduler/opencode-2/ws/app/cronlite/schedule.py","time":{"start":1794861188667,"end":1794861188676}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There's a bug! `next_run('0 0 30 2 *', datetime(2026,1,1,0,0))` returned 2026-02-01 instead of raising ValueError. And `0 0 29 2 *` gave consecutive days 2027-02-01, 02-02, 02-03 — wrong.\n\nThe bug: `_matches_day` — dom restricted? DOM field text is \"30\" → restricted=True. DOW field text is \"*\" → dow_restricted = False. So the code path `if self._dom_restricted: return day_of_week_ok` — wait, that's wrong!\n\nLet me re-read the spec: \"Day of month and day of week combine as in classic cron: when both fields are restricted (neither is `*`), a day matches if *either* matches; when one of them is `*`, only the other counts.\"\n\nSo when DOM is restricted (\"30\") and DOW is \"*\" → only DOM counts. My code has it backwards: `if self._dom_restricted: return day_of_week_ok` returns the DOW match when DOM is restricted. It should be the opposite:\n\n- dom restricted and dow restricted → dom_ok or dow_ok\n- dom restricted (dow is \"*\") → dom_ok\n- dow restricted (dom is \"*\") → dow_ok\n- neither restricted → True\n\nLet me fix: \n```python\nif self._dom_restricted and self._dow_restricted:\n    return day_of_month_ok or day_of_week_ok\nif self._dom_restricted:\n    return day_of_month_ok\nif self._dow_restricted:\n    return day_of_week_ok\nreturn True\n```\n\nYes, I had the two branches swapped. Fix it.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e6104626001bdCV1l2paLolaB","sessionID":"ses_e19f1290fffeOm13DSw4yBRd3L","messageID":"msg_1e610391900190QpyC6a8fiCT0"}}
