ser.py (field grammar, validation, DOM/DOW star detection)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement cronlite/schedule.py (next-fire computation with 8-year horizon)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement cronlite/__init__.py public API (next_run)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement cronlite/__main__.py CLI (--after, --count, exit code 2 on errors)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write tests (unittest, stdlib only) covering parsing, semantics, CLI","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write README.md and pyproject.toml; run full test suite","status":"pending","priority":"medium"}],"truncated":false},"title":"2 todos","time":{"start":1794861193417,"end":1794861193420}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All correct now. Jan 2 2026 — let me verify the weekday: 2026-01-01 is a Thursday, so Jan 2 is a Friday. ✓ (cron dow 5 = Friday.)\n\nNow let me update the todos and write the tests.\n\nTests to write:\n1. Parsing valid expressions and their value sets.\n2. Invalid expressions → ValueError.\n3. next_run basic behavior: strictly after, seconds/microseconds ignored, result zeroed.\n4. DOM/DOW combination semantics.\n5. Never-firing → ValueError.\n6. CLI: output format, count, --after, exit code 2 for invalid expression and invalid --after.\n7. Randomized cross-check: compare next_run against a brute-force minute-by-minute scan for a bunch of expressions.\n\nThe brute-force cross-check is a great way to validate the stepping algorithm. I'll write it in the test file (minute-by-minute iteration, capped).\n\nLet me write the test file.\n\nFor the brute force check, I need an independent matcher. I'll write a simple matcher in the test that checks minute/hour/month/day sets and DOM/DOW rules using the parsed field values from `cronlite.parse` — but using a different combination approach. That's OK, since the day-of-month/day-of-week logic is separately tested.\n\nLet me write tests/test_cronlite.py and tests/test_cli.py.\n\nFor the CLI test, use subprocess with sys.executable and cwd = project root, env PYTHONPATH set to project root.\n\nLet me write the tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e61058c3001afEepH2Cga3m0G","sessionID":"ses_e19f1290fffeOm13DSw4yBRd3L","messageID":"msg_1e6104c41001bax6TBLct1I4Ux"}}
