s... no, `rand_field` for hours picks from star/num/range/step/step_range/list. \"step\" gives e.g. */12 → 2 values. Lists give up to 3 ranges → up to 24 values.\n\nHmm, 3000 iterations × up to 2928 days × ... 0.35s total seems too fast. Let me check that the loop is actually running 3000 times — `checked` printed 3000. And for each, brute() scans. For a random expression, the first matching day is usually found within a few days (most fields have few values), so the day loop is short. The inner hours×minutes loop only runs for matching days. So it's plausible.\n\nBut wait — for the case where the expression never fires (e.g. dom=31, month=2), the brute force scans all 2928 days → slower but not too bad.\n\nLet me increase the sample size and also test the \"never fires\" path more. Also let me double check the fuzz covers expressions that never fire — yes, e.g. \"31 2\" combos.\n\nLet me run with more iterations and a different seed for extra confidence.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e611b3e0001Kc21r5Qj2kTnb0","sessionID":"ses_e19f1290fffeOm13DSw4yBRd3L","messageID":"msg_1e611a62e001KX6fQpbfazC2MY"}}
