CronError, ValueError)` — CronError is redundant; keep just ValueError? But explicitly listing CronError documents intent. Ruff didn't complain (B014 would flag redundant exceptions, but it wasn't triggered... actually flake8-bugbear B014 \"redundant exception types\" — ruff's default rules don't include B). Let me simplify to `except ValueError` since CronError is a ValueError subclass. But then the CronError import becomes unused → remove it.\n\nLet me make these two edits.\n\nAlso `_TIME_FORMAT` would become unused → remove or keep for the strftime fallback. I'll remove it and use the f-string formatting.\n\nLet me also reconsider the `--after` accepting a space separator: keep it (documented? The README doesn't mention it). Let me add a line to the README noting that a space is accepted in place of \"T\". Actually the README shows the format as YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM. I'll add a brief note.\n\nLet me make the changes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e612ebe1001BQCkzSWc30w3jL","sessionID":"ses_e19f1290fffeOm13DSw4yBRd3L","messageID":"msg_1e612dd33001NEkDGapEbAvwW7"}}
